2. Notification triggers

You must notify the upstream project before either of the following begins:

(a) Commercial Use: using or distributing the Software as part of a product,
    service, offering, or activity primarily intended for commercial advantage
    or monetary compensation. Examples include selling copies, incorporating
    the Software into a commercial product, and offering a paid or monetized
    service based on the Software.
(b) Modified Distribution: publishing or distributing a modified source or
    binary version of the Software to third parties, whether free or paid.

Ordinary installation and private end-user use do not require notification,
including ordinary workplace use of the quota display. Private modifications
that are not distributed or used for Commercial Use do not require notification.
Changing local preferences alone is not Modified Distribution. Sharing the
unmodified Software without Commercial Use does not require notification.

3. How to notify

Create a GitHub Issue at the upstream project's notification tracker:
https://github.com/vence15008-ai/codex-quota-header-public/issues

Use a title beginning with "[Usage notice]" and provide:
- the project or product name;
- a short, non-confidential description of the purpose;
- whether the notice covers Commercial Use, Modified Distribution, or both;
- a public project or product link, if one is available.

One notice per distinct project or commercial offering is sufficient, including
when both triggers apply. Routine updates within the described scope do not
require repeated notices. A materially different project or offering requires
a new notice. No source-code disclosure, revenue report, legal name, private
contact details, credentials, or confidential business information is required.

Notification is complete when the Issue is submitted. You do not need approval
or acknowledgment and do not need to wait for a reply. Notification creates no
payment obligation, endorsement, or support obligation. If the tracker cannot
accept your Issue, keep a dated record of the attempted notice and submit it
when the tracker can accept it again; no approval or fee is required meanwhile.
Submitting a contribution directly to the upstream project by Issue or pull
request needs no separate usage notice for that contribution itself. This does
not substitute for notice of an independent commercial offering or release.

